LESSON 1: CONNECTING TO THE BACK END
UNDERSTANDING SIDE EFFECTS, HOOKS AND useEffect
================================================================================
PART 1: OVERVIEW OF THE LESSON
================================================================================

WHAT YOU'LL LEARN IN THIS LESSON
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This lesson introduces React side effects and the useEffect Hook.

You will understand:

• What side effects are

• What React Hooks are

• What useEffect does

• When useEffect is appropriate

• When useEffect is NOT necessary

• How dependency arrays work

• How effect cleanup works

• How to fetch data from a backend

• How to manage loading state

• How to manage error state

• How to cancel obsolete HTTP requests

• How to avoid race conditions

• How effects run during component lifecycle

• How to keep rendering logic pure


WHY THIS LESSON IS IMPORTANT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

So far, most Grocery List behavior has happened entirely inside React.

Examples:

Add Item
Toggle Item
Delete Item
Calculate Statistics


These operations use:

React State
     ↓
React Rendering
     ↓
UI


Real applications also interact with systems outside React.

Examples:

React Application
      ↓
HTTP Request
      ↓
Backend API
      ↓
Database
      ↓
HTTP Response
      ↓
React State
      ↓
UI


The important concept is:

RENDERING
+
SIDE EFFECTS


Rendering determines:

WHAT THE UI SHOULD LOOK LIKE


